  fighting the south carolina started to  gain the upper hand  at one point towards the end bonnet  allegedly wanted to  blow up his ship rather than be captured  but he was stopped by his men who  decided to surrender ultimately steed  bonnet and 33 of his men survived the  battle were arrested  and taken to charlestown as a gentleman  bonnet was given preferential treatment  and was  allowed to stay in the house of the  provost marshal on october 24th he  actually managed to escape but was  only at large for four days before being  captured again his men  didn't have it so good after 33 29 were  found guilty of piracy and sentenced to  death and  they were all hanged on november the 8th  a few days later bonnet's trial took  place and  he too was found guilty and sentenced to  die his date of execution  was scheduled for december the 10th so  bonnet still had some  time to try and evade his ghastly fate  he begged  he argued he pleaded he tried blaming  blackbeard he  wrote letters to anyone who would listen  attempt to get his sentence commuted  he managed to gain a lot of public  sympathy and even his captor colonel  rhett  was moved to the point that he offered  to travel with bonnet to england for a  new trial the gentleman pirate  used his pleas and his tears to move  everyone  except for the one person who mattered  governor johnson  despite public pressure the governor  remained steadfast in his decision  arguing that bonnet had already broken  his word once so on december 10th an  almost insensible steed bonnet was  dragged to the gallows and in front of a  crowd that exhibited more pity  than contempt or hatred he was hanged  nowadays a historical marker is  all that remains of the spot where the  notorious gentleman pirate and  29 of his men met their end so i really  hope you found that video interesting if  you did please do hit that thumbs up  button below also do subscribe  also check out my new channel side  projects linked to below  and thank you f